#
# prima-materia — New Thought: Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken
# Word (1945)
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:NewThought, kept apart from
# traditions/new-thought.ttl, which declares the tradition and its works
# (pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord is declared there, not here). The whole
# book was read, pp. 238-299, in the order of its nine chapters; the nodes
# follow the chapters and, within each, the place in the text that carries
# them. Every source names the chapter title as the chapter heading gives it
# (the contents page of the text layer garbles ch. 2 as "-1 Give").
#
# The book was published after the author's death (1940) as a compilation of
# her notes and memoranda; the eBook's title note says they were gathered by a
# student, who is not named, and the foreword, p. 240, is signed by Emmet Fox.
# The text read is not the 1945 print. It is Book Four of the eBook "The
# Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn" (eBook edition copyright 2007,
# www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com), pp. 238-299, whose page numbers stand on
# their own line at the foot of each page. Two archive.org uploads of this
# eBook were read as mutual witnesses: TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn
# for the text and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn, a second OCR of the
# same pages, where the first is garbled ("Finked" p. 248, "Laith" and
# "World's Lair" p. 289). The DeVorss print (archive.org
# powerofspokenwor0000shin, 1978) and the printed collection
# completeworksoff0000flor are access-restricted and were not read, so whether
# the eBook keeps the wording and order of 1945 is unchecked; every source
# says so.
#
# Every record of this harvest was compared with the Scovel Shinn nodes of
# traditions/new-thought-game-of-life.ttl, traditions/new-thought-your-word-
# is-your-wand.ttl, traditions/new-thought-secret-door-to-success.ttl and
# traditions/new-thought.ttl. Where a node there carries the same being,
# practice, caution or capacity, no node is written here and links point at
# it:
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnAFriendlyAiredale,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnAnswerToHisPrayerManifest,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnAppearanceOfEvilEvaporates,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnArmyOfTheAliens, pmp:NewThoughtShinnBeUndisturbed,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnBlessingsComeAsGifts,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnCallingOnTheLaw,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnChangeYourConditions,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnConditionsPermanentlyPerfect,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteLeadReceived, pmp:NewThoughtShinnDenyingLoss,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDepreciationAndFearOfLoss,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDivineDesign,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnDominionOverTheElements,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnEternalYouth,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnFallsAwayOfItsOwnWeight,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnFeelRichAndSuccessful,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnForcingCareers, pmp:NewThoughtShinnGoodWill,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnHoldingTheVisionForAnother,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnHoldingWrongMentalPictures,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnIFulfillMyDestiny, pmp:NewThoughtShinnILookWithWonder,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnIdleWords, pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFaculty,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnImmediateAndEndlessSupply,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnImpatientDesires, pmc:NewThoughtShinnIncreaseUnderGrace,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnInfiniteIntelligence, pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuition,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionIsGodTelephoning,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnInvertedFaith,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnLeaveThePlanToTheDivineDesigner,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnMessageOrLead, pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyFatherInHeaven,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnNegativeThoughtsStarveOnFaith,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnObstaclesSpringBoards,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnOccultLawOfIndifference,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnOnlyOnePower, pmc:NewThoughtShinnPerfectSelfExpression,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnPersonalWill, pmc:NewThoughtShinnRaceThought,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnRadioActivity,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnRealizationIsManifestation,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnRealmOfPerfectIdeas, pmc:NewThoughtShinnRubOutMistakes,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingImpossibleDoorsOpen,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnShowActiveFaith, pmc:NewThoughtShinnStillSmallVoice,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnSubconsciousMind, pmc:NewThoughtShinnSuperconsciousMind,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheBattleIsWon,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPass,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDesiresOfMyHeart,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnTooCloseToOwnAffairs,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnWalkingUpToTheLion,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnWallsOfLackAndDelay,
# pmp:NewThoughtShinnWavingOverItTheWandOfHisWord,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhateverIShouldKnowRevealed,
# pmc:NewThoughtShinnYouCombineWithWhatYouNotice.
# Where this book states a claim of those files differently, the node carries
# a note beginning "Differs from".
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#924 with two independent extraction passes
# over the text (A 502 records, B 419; 9 records of B without counterpart in
# A: 0 added, 9 covered, 0 not owed), then integrated by a reader of the whole
# text, who added 2 records both passes missed. Identifiers are
# pmc:NewThoughtShinn or pmp:NewThoughtShinn plus the author's own wording in
# PascalCase. Signs of success, conditions of failure and capacities carry a
# note beginning "Counted as". Cases the author tells of clients and others
# are entered as third-party ascriptions, her own as first-person reports.
# The one reception claim is the words that came to a woman in England,
# p. 248; the scripture and hymn lines the author puts in God's mouth are not
# reception claims.
#

#
# Title note
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCompendiumOfNotesGatheredByAStudent a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Compilation of the author's notes into nine chapters"@en, "Zusammenstellung der Notizen der Autorin in neun Kapitel"@de ;
    skos:definition "An unnamed student compiled Shinn's notes and memoranda after her death into a foreword plus nine scripture-headed chapters; most chapters close with a free-standing affirmation or verse."@en ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the compiler's, not the author's: the foreword is signed by Emmet Fox and the compiler is not named. The chapter titles are biblical phrases."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "An unnamed student of the author, by the title note of the eBook (\"gathered by a student\"); the foreword is signed by Emmet Fox" ;
    dcterms:date "1945"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, title note, p. 238; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

#
# Chapter 1, Weapons Ye Know Not Of
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWeaponsYeKnowNotOf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "God works through unforeseen weapons, ways and channels"@en, "Gott wirkt durch unvorhergesehene Waffen, Wege und Kanäle"@de ;
    skos:definition "The answer to prayer is held to come through means the petitioner cannot foresee; the Divine is credited with ingenuity and sure methods."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTellSupremeIntelligenceJustHow a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not prescribe to God how the prayer is to be answered"@en, "Gott nicht vorschreiben, wie das Gebet zu erhören ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting to know the channel in advance and giving Infinite Intelligence exact directions is said to limit the Divine working."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnWeaponsYeKnowNotOf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhenYePrayBelieveYeHaveIt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Pray believing you already have it, with a child's expectancy"@en, "Beten im Glauben, es schon zu haben, mit kindlicher Erwartung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When praying, hold that the thing asked for is already received; wait for it in joyful expectancy like a child before Christmas, sleeping untroubled rather than agonizing over whether it will come."@en ;
    skos:note "Interpreted gospel saying on believing one has received, plus the drum illustration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWhenYePrayBelieveYeHaveItYieldsAnswerToHisPrayerManifest a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Expectant believing prayer yields answered prayer"@en, "Erwartungsvolles Glaubensgebet bewirkt Erhörung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paraphrased scripture: child-like expectancy is said to bring the answer."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhenYePrayBelieveYeHaveIt ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnAnswerToHisPrayerManifest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSleeplessNightsAgonizing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sleepless agonizing over the channel and the timing"@en, "Schlaflose Sorge um Kanal und Zeitpunkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The adult who lies awake wondering how and whether the money will arrive in time, while professing faith, shows the lack of trust that blocks the answer."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhenYePrayBelieveYeHaveIt fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyWaysAreIngenious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Answer heard: inventive ways and reliable methods"@en, "Vernommene Antwort: meine Wege sind findig, meine Methoden sicher"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the anxious petitioner's doubt, the text gives an answer in the first person of God promising unknown weapons and inventive, reliable methods."@en ;
    skos:note "The first sentence repeats the opening quotation of the chapter; the second has no named speaker and is not given as a verse, so it is entered as the author's own teaching and not as a received wording."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 241; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnCommittingYourWaysUntoTheLord a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Commit your ways to the Lord by following intuition"@en, "Dem Herrn die Wege anbefehlen, indem man der Intuition folgt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hand the matter over to God, which in practice means acting on intuitive promptings (hunches) instead of planning by reason."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCommittingYourWaysUntoTheLordYieldsTheDemonstrationComesToPass a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following intuition yields the demonstration by the shortest route"@en, "Intuition folgen bewirkt die Demonstration auf kürzestem Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Intuition is called the magic path and the beeline to the demonstration."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnCommittingYourWaysUntoTheLord ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPass ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDespiseNotTheDayOfSmallThings a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not despise small things"@en, "Kleine Dinge nicht verachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "With intuition nothing counts as unimportant; seemingly trivial events and prompts must be heeded."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnDayOfSmallThings (The Game of Life, p. 52): there the warning is not to scorn small first results of a demonstration; here it is not to dismiss seemingly trivial events and prompts, since with intuition nothing is unimportant."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnCommittingYourWaysUntoTheLord ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRegularHabits a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Reasoners and creatures of habit find intuition hard"@en, "Verstandesmenschen und Gewohnheitstiere tun sich mit Intuition schwer"@de ;
    skos:definition "People who have always followed reason, and those with rigid daily routines who are upset by any deviation, are warned that switching to intuitive guidance is difficult for them."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnCommittingYourWaysUntoTheLord ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPowerOfChoice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two roads: intuition or hard experience"@en, "Zwei Wege: Intuition oder harte Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans may choose intuition's magic route or the lengthy, hard way of experience that comes from following the reasoning mind; following the superconscious leads to the heights."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnPictureOfEternalYouthAndEternalLife a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Impress the subconscious with an image of unending youth and life"@en, "Dem Unterbewusstsein das Bild ewiger Jugend und ewigen Lebens einprägen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take the image of unending youth and deathless life found in the intuition and stamp it on the subconscious, which then executes it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 242; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPictureOfEternalYouthAndEternalLifeYieldsEternalYouth a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Impressing eternal youth yields a deathless body"@en, "Einprägen ewiger Jugend bewirkt unsterblichen Leib"@de ;
    skos:definition "The subconscious carries out the idea and the body is said to be transmuted."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnPictureOfEternalYouthAndEternalLife ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnEternalYouth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
