pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheLordOrLaw a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Lord as Law; King of Glory"@en, "Der Herr als Gesetz; König der Herrlichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Lord is glossed as the Law; the King of Glory is the incoming perfect idea that routs negative thoughts."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"the Lord (or Law)\"."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "The Lord (or Law); King of Glory" ;
    pm:nameRole "lawful divine power acting in consciousness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 243; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBibleIsTalkingAboutStatesOfConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Bible speaks of thoughts and states of consciousness"@en, "Die Bibel spricht von Gedanken und Bewusstseinszuständen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interpretive key used throughout: biblical gates, kings, enemies and battles are read as mental contents; in Psalm 24 the gates opening are perfect superconscious ideas entering the conscious mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
