pmc:NewThoughtShinnFlashesAcrossYourConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A flash of a seemingly impossible good"@en, "Ein Aufblitzen von etwas zu Schönem, um wahr zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Divine Idea of one's life is said often to flash across consciousness as something seemingly too good to be true; read as a sign that the true plan is showing itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text names it as a mark that the work has taken effect. Counted apart from conditions of failure. It is announced as a mark of pmc:NewThoughtShinnExpandingRapidlyIntoTheDivinePlan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 1 \"Weapons Ye Know Not Of\", p. 244; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPlaceYouWereDestinedToFill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Destiny: the place one was meant to fill; full equipment for it"@en, "Bestimmung: der vorgesehene Platz; volle Ausrüstung dafür"@de ;
    skos:definition "Few fulfil their destinies; yet everyone is held to be completely furnished for the Divine Plan and above any situation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
