#
# Chapter 2, I Give Unto You Power
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGodsGiftToManIsPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Power as God's gift; unhappiness from lack of power"@en, "Macht als Gottes Gabe; Unglück aus Machtlosigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "God gave man power and dominion over mind, body and affairs; all unhappiness stems from lacking power; alone man is a victim of circumstance, joined with God-power all is possible."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEveryBurdenIsLifted a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every burden lifted, every battle won"@en, "Jede Last gehoben, jede Schlacht gewonnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through contact with God-power, burdens are said to be removed miraculously and battles won."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCallingOnTheLawYieldsEveryBurdenIsLifted a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The word yields lifted burdens"@en, "Das Wort bewirkt gehobene Lasten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that the practice \"Making conscious contact with the Invincible Power by one's word\" brings about \"Every burden lifted, every battle won\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnCallingOnTheLaw ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnEveryBurdenIsLifted ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
