pmc:NewThoughtShinnOvercomingMeansToConquer a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Overcoming: conquering doubt, fear and negative vibrations"@en, "Überwinden: Zweifel, Furcht und negative Schwingungen besiegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Overcoming means mastering doubts, fears and negative vibrations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDissolveAllNegativeVibrations a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dissolving all negative vibrations by one poised loving person"@en, "Auflösen aller negativen Schwingungen durch einen gefassten, liebenden Menschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A single person in perfect peace and poise, full of love and good will, could melt all negative vibrations like snow in sun."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnEvilIsUnrealAndLeavesNoStainThanksgiving a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Give thanks that heaven on earth is coming to pass; evil leaves no stain"@en, "Danken, dass der Himmel auf Erden geschieht; das Böse hinterlässt keinen Fleck"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give thanks now for the fulfilment of the power to bring heaven to earth, holding evil to be unreal and markless."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation-style thanksgiving built on a gospel saying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGodPower a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God-power"@en, "Gotteskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Divine power located within the person as the superconscious mind; realm of inspiration, revelation, illumination, miracles and wonders; source of all real power."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"God-power\"."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "God-power" ;
    pm:nameRole "indwelling divine power, worked with by the word" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 247; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingImpossibleDoorsOpenPresupposesIntuitionFliesOutOfTheWindow a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Yield to God-power and quiet reason"@en, "Der Gotteskraft Vorfahrt geben und den Verstand stillen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Working with God-power requires first yielding to it and quieting reason."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeemingImpossibleDoorsOpen ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionFliesOutOfTheWindow ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
