pmc:NewThoughtShinnActHisFaith a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Infinite Intelligence knows the way; man rejoices, thanks and acts his faith"@en, "Die Unendliche Intelligenz kennt den Weg; der Mensch freut sich, dankt und handelt im Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Division of labour: the moment one asks, the way of fulfilment is known above; the human part is rejoicing, thanksgiving and acting on faith."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 248; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnActAsThoughIWereAndIAm a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Words received: act as if I were present, then I am"@en, "Empfangene Worte: handle, als wäre ich, und ich bin"@de ;
    skos:definition "A well-known Englishwoman, praying intensely for a realization of God, reported these words coming to her."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "An unnamed English woman of some renown, whose experience the author retells" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Not named; the words answer her asking for a realization of God and speak in the first person of the one she sought" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "By the author's retelling, p. 248: the words came to her while she prayed earnestly to realize God; nothing is said of her state, of anyone questioning her or writing the words down, and no record other than this retelling is mentioned. The author uses the words to back her rule that the subconscious is impressed by faith acted out, and by nothing else." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 248; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPassPresupposesBuyLittleThingsForIt a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "No results without impressing the subconscious by active faith"@en, "Keine Ergebnisse ohne Einprägung ins Unterbewusstsein durch tätigen Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only faith expressed in action impresses the subconscious, and without that impression nothing happens."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPass ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnBuyLittleThingsForIt ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "There are no results." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 248; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnBuyLittleThingsForIt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Act your faith: prepare as if the good were already coming"@en, "Den Glauben ausleben: so vorbereiten, als käme das Gute schon"@de ;
    skos:definition "Take concrete steps that presuppose the answer, e.g. buy things for the hoped-for home as if no time were left, while appearances say otherwise."@en ;
    skos:note "Instance of the active-faith rule; from the right-marriage case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 248; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnImmuneToAllHurtAndResentment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation of immunity to hurt and resentment"@en, "Affirmation der Unverletzlichkeit gegen Kränkung und Groll"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declare present immunity to every hurt and grudge, one's poise resting on the rock of the Christ within; perfect oneself in the situation until no grudge remains."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation given to a client."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 2 \"I Give Unto You Power\", p. 248; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappyHomeCameIntoManifestationPresupposesImmuneToAllHurtAndResentment a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Immunity to hurt before the man or his equivalent is given"@en, "Unverletzlichkeit vor der Gabe des Mannes oder seines Gegenstücks"@de ;
    skos:definition "She told the client the man, or an equivalent, would come once she was immune to hurt and resentment."@en ;
    skos:note "The text adds the proviso that the man may be given or his equivalent."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnHappyHomeCameIntoManifestation ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnImmuneToAllHurtAndResentment ;
