#
# Chapter 3, Be Strong; Fear Not
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFaceDefeatWheneverFearful a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear brings defeat and attracts the feared thing"@en, "Furcht bringt Niederlage und zieht das Gefürchtete an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whenever fearful one faces defeat, loses all power, and magnetizes the thing feared."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 254; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGreyHairReturnedToItsNaturalColor a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Case: grey hair regained natural color when worry stopped"@en, "Fall: graues Haar bekam wieder seine Farbe, als die Sorge endete"@de ;
    skos:definition "A hairdresser reported a client of hers whose grey hair regained its original color after she ceased worrying."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 254; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWalkingUpToTheLionYieldsGreyHairReturnedToItsNaturalColor a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing worry restored hair color (reported case)"@en, "Aufhören zu sorgen gab dem Haar die Farbe zurück (berichteter Fall)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, friend or acquaintance: the practice \"Walking up to the lion\" was followed by the outcome \"grey hair regained natural color when worry stopped\"."@en ;
    skos:note "Practice linked is facing the fear; text only says she stopped worrying."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnWalkingUpToTheLion ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnGreyHairReturnedToItsNaturalColor ;
