pmc:NewThoughtShinnCrystallizedThought a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every negative situation is crystallized thought"@en, "Jede negative Lage ist kristallisierter Gedanke"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bad situations are built from one's own vain imaginings and cannot withstand the light of Truth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 255; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCannotStandTheLightOfTruth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Negative situations dissolve in the light of Truth"@en, "Negative Lagen lösen sich im Licht der Wahrheit auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Negative situations, being crystallized thought, are said to give way once Truth is brought to bear on them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
