pmp:NewThoughtShinnTheLordIsMyLightAndSalvation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Face the situation fearlessly with Psalm 27"@en, "Der Lage furchtlos mit Psalm 27 begegnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meet the negative situation without fear, speaking the line that the Lord is one's light and salvation, so none need be feared."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation from scripture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 255; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDefiniteRulesForControllingConditions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus as greatest metaphysician with definite rules"@en, "Jesus als größter Metaphysiker mit bestimmten Regeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jesus is said to have given definite rules for controlling conditions by word and thought."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnGreatestOfMetaphysicians (The Secret Door to Success, p. 211): there Jesus is the greatest metaphysician because he knew the law of supply; here because he gave definite rules for ruling conditions by word and thought."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 255; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnWordOfAuthority a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Counter each negative thought with an authoritative word"@en, "Jedem negativen Gedanken mit einem Wort der Vollmacht antworten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Be wiser than the enemy thoughts: whenever a negative thought arises, reply at once with a counter-statement, and keep this up for as long as needed, monotonously like katydids."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 255; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSupplyLikeMushroomsOvernight a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Affirmation: divine supply springing up like mushrooms"@en, "Affirmation: meine Versorgung kommt von Gott und erscheint wie Pilze"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reply to the thought that business is dull and money scarce with the statement that one's supply is from God and springs up overnight; no hard times in the kingdom."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation, as counter-statement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
