pmc:NewThoughtShinnAdamicDreamOfOpposites a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Adamic dream of opposites; the fall as rise of reasoning mind"@en, "Der adamitische Traum der Gegensätze; der Fall als Aufkommen des Verstandes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adam (Generic Mind) ate from Illusion's tree and slept, imagining good and evil; in Eden man worked only from the superconscious and was provided for; reasoning brought lack and toil. Jesus came to wake people up."@en ;
    skos:note "Supported by a quotation from Bernard Shaw, Back to Methuselah, used approvingly."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnAdamicDream (The Secret Door to Success, p. 230): there the dream is of two powers, good and evil; here the fall is the rise of the reasoning mind, Eden being the stage in which man worked from the superconscious only."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 3 \"Be Strong; Fear Not\", p. 256; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGardenOfEdenConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth dimension as Eden consciousness"@en, "Vierte Dimension: das Bewusstsein des Gartens Eden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jesus' message is said to return people to the fourth-dimensional Eden consciousness; John 14 sums up His teaching."@en ;
    skos:note "Author's term: \"fourth dimension\"."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
