#
# Chapter 4, The Glory of the Lord
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGloryIsTheLawInAction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Glory as radiance: the law in action"@en, "Herrlichkeit als Glanz: das Gesetz in Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Glory means radiance, i.e. the law working visibly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 4 \"The Glory of the Lord\", p. 261; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGodIsPrinciple a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God as Principle, Power, Supreme Intelligence within"@en, "Gott als Prinzip, Macht, Höchste Intelligenz im Innern"@de ;
    skos:definition "God cannot be seen because God is Principle; what is seen are the proofs of God."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "God; Principle; Power; Supreme Intelligence" ;
    pm:nameRole "impersonal principle known by its proofs" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
