pmc:NewThoughtShinnCriticalPeopleAreAlwaysCriticized a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Critical people are criticized and get rheumatism"@en, "Kritische Menschen werden kritisiert und bekommen Rheuma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Living in the vibration of criticism brings criticism back; acid thoughts are said to make acid blood and joint pain."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnRefrainsFromCriticizing fails."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnRheumatismCorrespondence (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 67): there rheumatism simply corresponds to fault-finding; here it is one of two returns of criticism, the other being that the critic is criticized in turn."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 4 \"The Glory of the Lord\", p. 262; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBoilingWithin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily symptoms as images of emotions"@en, "Körperliche Symptome als Abbilder von Gefühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illness mirrors inner states: boils in a woman whenever her mother-in-law visited (inner boiling, from a newspaper report of a physician), skin trouble when someone has got under one's skin, rheumatism from acid thinking."@en ;
    skos:note "The boils case is reported via a newspaper article; she adds that not all mothers-in-law bring discord."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 4 \"The Glory of the Lord\", p. 262; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

