pmc:NewThoughtShinnNowIsTheAppointedTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Now is the appointed time; past and future rob time"@en, "Jetzt ist die rechte Zeit; Vergangenheit und Zukunft rauben Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation is today; the two thieves on the cross are said to stand for the robbers of time, past and future; worry and fear rob time; a Sanskrit poem bids one look to this day."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnLivingInThePast (The Game of Life, p. 35): there dwelling on the past is a method of failure; here the stress lies on today as the appointed time, with worry and fear also named as robbers of time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
