#
# Chapter 5, Peace and Prosperity
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPeaceAndProsperityGoHandInHand a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Peace and prosperity go together"@en, "Friede und Wohlstand gehen Hand in Hand"@de ;
    skos:definition "From Psalm 122: the peaceful person is wide awake, sees clearly, acts fast and never misses a chance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 267; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearAndConfusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Those showing lack are in fear and confusion and miss leads"@en, "Wer Mangel zeigt, ist in Angst und Verwirrung und verpasst Fingerzeige"@de ;
    skos:definition "Appearance of lack goes with fear and confusion, being asleep to one's good, missing leads and opportunities."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 267; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnPeacefulPersonIsWideAwake a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wide-awake clarity and quick action through peace"@en, "Hellwache Klarheit und rasches Handeln durch Frieden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Peace is said to make a person alert, clear in seeing and quick in acting, so that no opportunity slips past."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 267; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnSpeakingTheWordForAnother a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Speak the Word for another person"@en, "Für einen anderen Menschen das Wort sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The teacher speaks a treatment on behalf of the client (here combined with giving her book The Game of Life)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
