pmc:NewThoughtShinnOnlyTheEmotionsKeepYouFromReaping a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Emotions alone block the harvest"@en, "Nur die Gefühle hindern einen, die Ernte einzubringen"@de ;
    skos:definition "At high altitude all is peace and fields are white for harvest; emotions alone stand between a person and a crop of success, joy and plenty; doubt and fear bring failure, unhappiness and disease."@en ;
    skos:note "Image drawn from her own airplane flight from California."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 268; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnYearsTheEmotionsHaveRuined a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration of years ruined by emotions"@en, "Wiederherstellung der von Gefühlen verdorbenen Jahre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paraphrasing Joel, she promises restoration of the years the emotions destroyed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 268; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearOfFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of failure, the commonest fear, harms body and happiness"@en, "Versagensangst, die häufigste Angst, schadet Leib und Glück"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing a newspaper on psychological findings: at least three quarters of those examined fear failure; continued fear affects glands and digestion, brings nervous symptoms and destroys health."@en ;
    skos:note "Appeal to contemporary psychology via press report."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 268; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAlreadyPlantedOnYourPathway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What you desire is already on your pathway"@en, "Was man wünscht, liegt schon auf dem eigenen Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fearless mind attracts all good; before one calls, the answer is given; fear is faith in evil."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 5 \"Peace and Prosperity\", p. 268; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnInformationWillBeGiven a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Needed information given"@en, "Benötigte Auskunft wird gegeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "A new word may bring sudden realization; information one needs will be supplied."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
