#
# Chapter 6, Your Big Opportunity
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOnlyOneJudgeYourWord a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Your word is your only judge; every day is judgment day"@en, "Das eigene Wort ist der einzige Richter; jeder Tag ist Gerichtstag"@de ;
    skos:definition "By one's words one is justified or condemned; looking back shows happiness or disaster attracted through words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 272; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnEveryDayIsADayOfJudgment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the teaching of a final judgment at history's close"@en, "Gegen die Lehre vom Gericht am Ende der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "She contrasts the former teaching that judgment comes at the world's end with her view that each day is judgment day through one's words."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a dispute: the author rejects the view named; the other side is not read and is entered only as she reports it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 272; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSpeakingWhileAngryOrResentful a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not speak while angry or resentful"@en, "Nicht im Zorn oder Groll sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The worst mistakes are made speaking in anger, because so much ill feeling backs the words."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnEveryActCommittedWhileAngry (Your Word Is Your Wand, p. 35): there the warning is against acting in anger; here against speaking in anger, because of the ill feeling behind the words."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnCallingOnTheLaw ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 272; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnVibratoryPowerOfWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Words vibrate: one attracts what one utters"@en, "Schwingungskraft der Worte: was man ausspricht, zieht man an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who constantly talk of disease attract it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 272; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSpeakOfDisease a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Talking of disease brings disease"@en, "Reden über Krankheit bringt Krankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who keep talking about illness are said to draw illness to themselves, by the vibration of their words."@en ;
