pmc:NewThoughtShinnDoNotDescribeAnythingDestructive a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not describe destructive things: one merges with what one notices"@en, "Nichts Zerstörerisches beschreiben: man verbindet sich mit dem Beachteten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illustrated by hearsay at a beauty parlour, where a client spreading health anxieties left everyone wondering if they were well."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnYouCombineWithWhatYouNotice (The Secret Door to Success, p. 166): there merging with what one notices is a law; here it grounds a warning against describing anything destructive, such as illnesses and operations."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnYouCombineWithWhatYouNotice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnOnlyDoubtsFearsAndResentments a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only doubts, fears and resentments keep good away"@en, "Nur Zweifel, Ängste und Groll halten das Gute fern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubt, fear and resentment are named as the only things that hold one's good back."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFastenedItToYou a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resented injustice fastened to you and repeated"@en, "Übelgenommenes Unrecht haftet an und wiederholt sich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hating or resenting a situation binds it to oneself; an unforgiven injustice engraves a picture in the subconscious and recurs with others until one feels cursed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTransmutesInjusticeIntoJusticePresupposesMyGoodWillIsAStrongTower a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Only one way to neutralize the injustice picture"@en, "Nur ein Weg, das Bild des Unrechts zu neutralisieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The good-will stance is declared the sole remedy."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnTransmutesInjusticeIntoJustice ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnMyGoodWillIsAStrongTower ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "History repeats until one feels cursed with misfortune and injustice." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnMyGoodWillIsAStrongTower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Unmoved by injustice, sending good will; the good-will tower affirmation"@en, "Von Unrecht unberührt bleiben und Wohlwollen senden; Affirmation vom Turm des Wohlwollens"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remain wholly unmoved by the injustice, send good will to everyone involved, and declare that good will surrounds one like a strong tower and that one now turns enemies to friends, discord to harmony, injustice to justice."@en ;
    skos:note "Affirmation, combined with an inner stance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnHarmonyOutOfChaos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Case: student brought harmony out of business chaos"@en, "Fall: Schülerin brachte Harmonie in ihr geschäftliches Chaos"@de ;
    skos:definition "A student of the author's is reported to have brought order into her disordered business by the good-will statement."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 276; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnMyGoodWillIsAStrongTowerYieldsHarmonyOutOfChaos a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Good-will tower statement yielded harmony (case)"@en, "Turm-Affirmation bewirkte Harmonie (Fall)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, friend or acquaintance: the practice \"Unmoved by injustice, sending good will; the good-will tower affirmation\" was followed by the outcome \"student brought harmony out of business chaos\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnMyGoodWillIsAStrongTower ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnHarmonyOutOfChaos ;
