pmp:NewThoughtShinnLuckyNellie a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Call the person lucky; speak the word for right marriage divinely designed"@en, "Die Person glücklich nennen; das Wort für die rechte, göttlich geplante Ehe sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Replace pitying names with Lucky or Fortunate; speak the word for a divinely designed marriage that cannot be interfered with; persist in affirmations, with faith that God now grants the heart's desires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 6 \"Your Big Opportunity\", p. 277; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnLuckyNellieYieldsMrsNellie a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Persistent affirmations yielded the marriage (case)"@en, "Beharrliche Affirmationen bewirkten die Ehe (Fall)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, friend or acquaintance: the practice \"Call the person lucky; speak the word for right marriage divinely designed\" was followed by the outcome \"Nellie married, the demon of fear dissolved\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnLuckyNellie ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnMrsNellie ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
