pmc:NewThoughtShinnSupplyCameFromGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Firm subconscious conviction that supply is from God"@en, "Feste unbewusste Überzeugung, dass die Versorgung von Gott kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The point of the case: loss of anxiety and an established conviction made supply unfailing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 280; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFearAndAnxietyMakeAShortCircuit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear and anxiety short-circuit Infinite Intelligence"@en, "Angst und Sorge schließen die Unendliche Intelligenz kurz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Man is an instrument through which Infinite Intelligence expresses as success, health and abundance, unless fear makes a short circuit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnShortCircuit (The Secret Door to Success, p. 212): there the reasoning mind and personal will make the short circuit; here fear and anxiety do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 280; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnSeeYourselfReceiving a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith means seeing yourself receive"@en, "Glaube heißt, sich empfangen zu sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Circus artists achieve seemingly impossible acts because they believe they can and see themselves performing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 280; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPassPresupposesFeelingThatYouAreAlreadyThere a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "You cannot do what you cannot see yourself doing"@en, "Man kann nicht tun, was man sich nicht tun sieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doing a thing or filling a place requires first realizing oneself in it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheDemonstrationComesToPass ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnFeelingThatYouAreAlreadyThere ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The thing cannot be done or the place filled." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
