pmc:NewThoughtShinnChannelsForItToExpressItself a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God as Supreme Intelligence within, man as channel"@en, "Gott als Höchste Intelligenz im Innern, der Mensch als Kanal"@de ;
    skos:definition "God is the Supreme Intelligence in each person; humans are channels through which It expresses; God is Giver and creates His own channels."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnSupremeIntelligence (The Secret Door to Success, p. 211): there the Supreme Intelligence is devoted to man's supply; here it is within each person, man is its channel, and it makes its own channels."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Supreme Intelligence within each person" ;
    pm:nameRole "indwelling giver; man is its channel" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 282; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnBlockedTheDivinelyDesignedChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deciding how the prayer is answered blocks the channel"@en, "Festlegen, wie das Gebet erhört wird, blockiert den Kanal"@de ;
    skos:definition "Then people complain their prayers are never answered."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnPrayWithPraiseAndThanksgiving fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFreeFromAllClutchOrAnxiety a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from clutch and anxiety in desiring"@en, "Freiheit von Verkrampfung und Sorge beim Wünschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A wish sent out with the divine-plan proviso is said to leave one without strain or anxiety over it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnAccordingToTheDivinePlanOrItsEquivalentYieldsFreeFromAllClutchOrAnxiety a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Divine-plan proviso yields freedom from clutch"@en, "Vorbehalt des göttlichen Plans bewirkt Freiheit von Verkrampfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that the practice \"Ask under the divine plan, or for its equivalent\" brings about \"Freedom from clutch and anxiety in desiring\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnAccordingToTheDivinePlanOrItsEquivalent ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnFreeFromAllClutchOrAnxiety ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnAccordingToTheDivinePlanOrItsEquivalent a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ask under the divine plan, or for its equivalent"@en, "Unter dem göttlichen Plan bitten oder um das Gleichwertige"@de ;
    skos:definition "Send a sincere desire as prayer with the proviso that it be received if in the divine plan, otherwise its equivalent; part of the technique of praying aright."@en ;
    skos:note "Formula / affirmation; calls praying aright an art and a technique."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnForceAnythingNotDivinelyPlanned a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not force anything not divinely planned"@en, "Nichts erzwingen, was nicht göttlich geplant ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is warned against pushing for anything that is not part of the divine plan."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnAccordingToTheDivinePlanOrItsEquivalent ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
