pmc:NewThoughtShinnTwentyThirdAndHundredAndTwentyFirstPsalms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Psalms 23 and 121 as expressions of absolute security"@en, "Psalmen 23 und 121 als Ausdruck vollkommener Sicherheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Both convey complete security and were written by someone who had experienced spiritual law."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnProtectsGuidesAndProvides a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Divine protection, guidance and provision"@en, "Göttlicher Schutz, Führung und Versorgung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When wholly trusted, the inner God is said to shield, lead and supply."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
