pmc:NewThoughtShinnShowingFearlessFaith a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Showing fearless faith is the chief part of demonstrating"@en, "Furchtlosen Glauben zeigen ist der wichtigste Teil des Demonstrierens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The brass gates and iron bars of Isaiah 45 are self-made doubts, fears and resentments; like elephants held by a mere rope, people are fenced in by illusory doubt and fear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnGatesOfBrassAndBarsOfIron a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Brass gates and iron bars = one's doubts and fears"@en, "Eherne Tore und eiserne Riegel = die eigenen Zweifel und Ängste"@de ;
    skos:definition "The gates and bars that God promises to break are read as one's doubts, fears, resentments and anxieties, made by oneself out of a belief in evil."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "gates of brass; bars of iron" ;
    pm:nameRole "states of consciousness: doubts, fears, resentments and anxieties" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 283; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnRopeAroundTheirConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt and fear as a rope that keeps one from clear thinking"@en, "Zweifel und Angst als Seil, das vom klaren Denken abhält"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told through the wild elephants kept in an enclosure by a mere rope: doubt and fear are a rope drawn round one's consciousness, which one could step over but believes one cannot, so that clear thinking is barred; intuition is said to tell one to step over it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause. It names how pmp:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionYourCompass fails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", pp. 283-284; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionYourCompass a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Let intuition be your compass"@en, "Die Intuition zum Kompass machen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clear vision is like having a compass; intuition will always lead one out of the woods, even without one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 7 \"In Nothing Be Anxious\", p. 284; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionYourCompassYieldsOutOfTheWoods a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Intuition as compass yields the way out"@en, "Intuition als Kompass bewirkt den Ausweg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text holds that the practice \"Let intuition be your compass\" brings about \"Finding the way out of any difficulty\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnIntuitionYourCompass ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnOutOfTheWoods ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
