#
# Chapter 8, Fearlessness
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnTheBattleIsNotYoursButGods a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The battle is God's, not yours (Jehoshaphat)"@en, "Der Kampf ist Gottes, nicht deiner (Josaphat)"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Jehoshaphat story is read as the individual's: outnumbered by adverse appearances, one hears that one need not fight; the enemies are doubts, fears, criticisms and resentments, and the enemy destroyed itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:NewThoughtShinnBattleIsGods (The Game of Life, p. 49): there the superconscious fights man's battle and burdens are adverse thoughts; here the story of Jehoshaphat shows the enemy, one's doubts and fears, destroying itself while one praises."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
