pmc:NewThoughtShinnHarnessAndDirectThought a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Harnessing thought like electricity"@en, "Den Gedanken wie Elektrizität nutzbar machen"@de ;
    skos:definition "As Edison trusted electrical laws and built a dynamo to harness and direct the force, Jesus taught people to harness and direct thought; fear is as dangerous as uncontrolled current."@en ;
    skos:note "OCR 'World's Lair' for World's Fair."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 8 \"Fearlessness\", p. 289; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImaginationRunningWild a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A wild imagination building fear pictures"@en, "Eine wilde Phantasie, die Angstbilder baut"@de ;
    skos:definition "Imagination is called man's workshop; uncontrolled, it is compared to riding an unbroken horse."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:NewThoughtShinnImagingFaculty ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
