#
# Chapter 9, Victory and Fulfillment
#

pmc:NewThoughtShinnCrosswordPuzzle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life as crossword: the right word gives the answer"@en, "Das Leben als Kreuzworträtsel: das rechte Wort gibt die Lösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Altering one's words alters one's world, the word being one's world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 293; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnImBrokeImSick a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Declaring oneself broke or sick condemns one"@en, "'Ich bin pleite, ich bin krank' sagen verurteilt einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Destructive conversation returns to its speaker."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
