pmc:NewThoughtShinnCreedsAndCeremonies a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against creedal and ceremonial Christianity"@en, "Gegen bekenntnis- und zeremonienhaftes Christentum"@de ;
    skos:definition "She holds that Jesus' message survived about three centuries, then its healing fire was lost and replaced by creeds and ceremonies only half understood; the Truth movement revives a creedless primitive Christianity, which many clergy now also teach."@en ;
    skos:note "Two passages, ch. 9, pp. 294 and 296; the tradition opposed is named only as creed and ceremony."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a dispute: the author rejects the view named; the other side is not read and is entered only as she reports it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", pp. 294, 296; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

