    rdfs:label "Asking without belief does not receive"@en, "Bitten ohne Glauben empfängt nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beliefs and expectancies are impressed on the subconscious and executed; faith creates expectancy."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:NewThoughtShinnAnswerToHisPrayerManifest ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:NewThoughtShinnWhenYePrayBelieveYeHaveIt ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One will not receive." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 294; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

