pmc:NewThoughtShinnGatesAndDoorsSymbolizeConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gates and doors of Psalm 24 symbolize consciousness"@en, "Tore und Türen von Psalm 24 symbolisieren das Bewusstsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lifted up in consciousness one contacts the superconscious, the God within; the King of glory then lifts burdens, fights battles and solves problems."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 297; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnDoorsAndGatesLocked a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt, fear and apprehension lock the gates against one's good"@en, "Zweifel, Furcht und Besorgnis verschließen die Tore vor dem Guten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The average person finds it hard to let the King of glory in."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
