pmc:NewThoughtShinnHopeNothingHappensToInterfere a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Case: anxious hoping that nothing interferes brought a headache"@en, "Fall: ängstliches Hoffen, dass nichts dazwischenkommt, brachte Kopfschmerz"@de ;
    skos:definition "A student who repeatedly hoped nothing would prevent her attending an important reception woke that day with a severe headache of a kind she had not had for years; her doubts and fears attracted it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 297; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmp:NewThoughtShinnNothingCanInterfereWithGodsPerfectPlan a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Word spoken that God's perfect plan cannot be thwarted; preparing as if well"@en, "Das Wort sprechen, dass nichts Gottes vollkommenen Plan stören kann; sich vorbereiten, als wäre man gesund"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shinn spoke the word; the student, though barely able to move, prepared to go, cleaning her jewelry and readying her dress."@en ;
    skos:note "Spoken word plus active faith."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 297; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnFogLifting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Case: headache lifted like a fog by evening"@en, "Fall: Kopfschmerz wich am Abend wie ein Nebel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Late in the afternoon she felt a fog lifting from her consciousness, was perfectly well and enjoyed the reception."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 297; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnNothingCanInterfereWithGodsPerfectPlanYieldsFogLifting a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spoken word and preparation healed the headache (case)"@en, "Gesprochenes Wort und Vorbereitung heilten den Kopfschmerz (Fall)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Told as a case of a client, friend or acquaintance: the practice \"Word spoken that God's perfect plan cannot be thwarted; preparing as if well\" together with \"Act your faith: prepare as if the good were already coming\" was followed by the outcome \"headache lifted like a fog by evening\"."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:NewThoughtShinnNothingCanInterfereWithGodsPerfectPlan, pmp:NewThoughtShinnBuyLittleThingsForIt ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NewThoughtShinnFogLifting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 297; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWellByTonight a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Time limits in one's words delay the healing"@en, "Zeitgrenzen in den eigenen Worten verzögern die Heilung"@de ;
    skos:definition "She believes healing would have come sooner had the student not asked to be well by evening; we keep limiting ourselves by our words."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:NewThoughtShinnNothingCanInterfereWithGodsPerfectPlan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
