pmc:NewThoughtShinnBeInterested a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "To be interesting, be interested"@en, "Um interessant zu sein, interessiert sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "An enthusiastic man was the centre of attention and drew others to buy what he liked, gaining nothing material; interest equals enthusiasm."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:ScovelShinnPowerOfTheSpokenWord ;
    dcterms:source "Florence Scovel Shinn, The Power of the Spoken Word (1945), in The Writings of Florence Scovel Shinn, eBook ed. (www.Self-Improvement-eBooks.com, 2007), Book Four, ch. 9 \"Victory and Fulfillment\", p. 298; read in the archive.org text layers TheCompleteWorksOfFlorenceScovelShinn and the-writing-of-florence-scovel-shinn of this eBook; agreement with the 1945 print unchecked" .

pmc:NewThoughtShinnWithoutVitalInterests a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lack of vital interest; living on others' affairs"@en, "Mangel an lebendigem Interesse; vom Leben anderer zehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "People without interests keep the radio on all day and must be entertained."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that goes wrong or does not come, and its cause."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:NewThought ;
